  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Biodiversitetsprojekt i Marokko</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Key results to be achieved in Morocco, Tunisia, Egypt, Jordan:
&#x2022;	Young women and men have enhanced employability and engage in entrepreneurship
&#x2022;	Small and medium enterprises and entrepreneurships grow and create jobs through development of innovative solutions, scaling up of existing solutions and improved access to finance and technical assistance
&#x2022;	Human Rights are promoted and protected for and by youth through a systemic approach involving all human rights stakeholders, youth networks and youth alliances in support of reform efforts 
&#x2022;	Violence and torture targeting youth is prevented, free media is strengthened and gender equality is improved through legislative reform, capacity building and dialogue 

Justification for support:
&#x2022;	DAPP is aligned with Danish foreign policy interests in the region. DAPP is based on lessons learned from past programmes
&#x2022;	DAPP seeks to address the root causes of migration by creating better lives for young people through programmes that support human rights, inclusion and employment generation
&#x2022;	DAPP&#x2019;s Human Rights Based Approach will be continued and amplified as it has demonstrated good results 
&#x2022;	DAPP has a longstanding presence in the region, that has fostered well-established and successful cooperation between Danish and local partners

Major risks and challenges:
&#x2022;	Increasing political instability with potential for civil unrest will be addressed by monitoring the situation and taking appropriate action in close collaboration with partners.
&#x2022;	Worsening economic situation and potential for increased poverty and migration will be mitigated by the DAPP focus on economic and social exclusion of youth.
&#x2022;	Increasing authoritarian rule, repression of minorities, and abuse of power will be addressed by engaging with both human rights duty bearers and right holders.</narrative>
  </description>
